######################## Reverse i search back and forth################################
To enable Ctrl + S for forward search: 
You need to disable this flow control (XON/XOFF) feature by running the command stty -ixon in your terminal.

To make this change permanent: Add stty -ixon to your shell's startup file (e.g., ~/.bashrc for Bash or ~/.zshrc for Zsh) and then restart your terminal or run source ~/.bashrc

################ Analizing stack ######################

Low ------top stack------						________________
			args      b-> (0x7fffffffca50) 								|
			args buffer->0x7fffffffcaa0										|
									|																	|
								4096																|
					end buf->0x7fffffffdaa0									frame
					 canary->0x7fffffffdaa8 (end buf+0x8)			|
								 ->0x7fffffffdaac (end buf+0xc)			|
					retaddr->0x7fffffffdac8										|
					retaddr->0x7fffffffdacc										|
								rbp							 ___________________|
Higher---------------

################### GDB commands #########################
find [/search_query_size] start_addr, end_addr, addr_value

The size of each search query value.
b:bytes 
h:halfwords (two bytes) 
w:words (four bytes) 
g:giant words (eight bytes) 

Ex.
	find /h 0x7fffffffca50, +0x1000, 0x06d4

############ Setting a Watchpoint on a Memory Address
To watch a 4-byte integer at address 0x12345678:
	(gdb) watch *(int *)0x12345678

To watch a single byte at address 0xdeadbeef:
	(gdb) watch *(char *)0xdeadbeef

############ Source view
	(gdb) list <first_line_code>,<last_line_code>
				list <line_code>

########### List memory regions mapped by the specified process
	(gdb) info proc mappings

########### Modify memory contents using GDB
	(gdb) set *0x7fffffffdaa8 =0x41414141

########### Command GDB that could be useful
	(gdb) help info proc
	(gdb) info proc mapping
	(gdb) bt
	
